      "verdict": "minimal_reusable_part",
      "detail": "Candidate covers only AllocationHandle::is_null (B=0x140985f30, correct) with a simplified single-u64 handle view. It does NOT cover Allocation/AllocationHandle inner pointer, ChunkId, SparseInstanceBuffer, SparseInstanceBufferWriter, or the 32-instance-chunk machinery (32 of 53 PDB symbols). Merged: is_null semantics (word==0) retained; handle modeled as {word, allocation: Option<NonNull<Allocation>>} per hide/show/allocation_to_draw evidence. The candidate's observed_word==0 null check is consistent with the 8-byte stub; the rest is superseded by this WP2 reconstruction."
    },
    "key_facts": [
      "TypedStorageBuffer<T> is 40 bytes: {Buffer(2 qwords), length, byte_size, +1 gap}.",
      "gpu_write_ranges_nonoverlapping scales element-index ranges by size_of::<T>() (Brick=0x60, WoodenPlank=0x40) and issues one update_buffer_bytes; bumpalo arena is a temp-only allocation detail.",
      "ShadowedBuffer<T> embeds DirtyIndexRange (AtomicUsize start/end, INCLUSIVE, empty=(MAX,0)) + Vec<T>(ptr,len) + TypedStorageBuffer<T> (72 bytes). gpu_flush uploads [start..=end] and clears.",
      "DirtyIndexRange.add = fetch_min(start) + fetch_max(end) (O deps).",
      "SparseInstanceBuffer<T> uses 32-instance chunks, byte_map of active counts (len=chunk_count+1, sentinel 0x20), active+dirty AtomicUsize bitmaps (len=chunk_count/64), free-chunk u32 stack, per-type chunk_count (RoofTile=0x2000, Brick/WoodenPlank=0x10000, Sparkle=0x6000).",
      "SparseInstanceBufferWriter.push writes into the current chunk until full (byte_map count==32), then pops a fresh chunk from the free stack; clear resets current_chunk to the full sentinel and returns claimed chunks.",
      "hide/show toggle active bits; take_out_waste reclaims freed allocations at gpu_flush start; gpu_flush uploads dirty chunk ranges via gpu_write_ranges_nonoverlapping.",
      "allocation_to_draw_multi_instanced / to_draw_multi_instanced build (start_slot,count) runs and return (0, 4, range_count) for the draw path.",
      "BufferWriteError has >=2 variants; Debug prints an Ok-like unit + Err-like 1-field tuple (impl$22::fmt)."
    ],
    "reuse_boundary": [
